  "category": "Feature",
  "description": "Audit & Standardize Receipt Print/Share Features, Add QZ Tray for Web\n\nAudit all existing receipt (struk) printing and sharing flows across both referenced features, then integrate QZ Tray SDK v2.x for direct thermal printing from the browser. Add paper size configuration (58mm / 80mm) in the settings page.\n\n**Phase 1 — Audit & Standardize**\n- Audit every output path in `feature-1781795898123-mse4d89oudj` and `feature-1781796894404-1fya40cv8ss`: browser print dialog, PDF generation, email attachment, WhatsApp share, and image share.\n- Document current receipt data schema, formatting inconsistencies, and layout differences across channels.\n- Define a single canonical receipt data model and unified layout template used by all output methods.\n\n**Phase 2 — QZ Tray Integration**\n- Integrate QZ Tray SDK v2.x into the web frontend for direct local-printer communication.\n- Implement auto-detection of the QZ Tray local service on page load; show an install prompt with download link if missing.\n- Build printer discovery flow, a printer-selection UI (dropdown or list), and a live connection-status indicator.\n- Configure digital certificate signing (QZ Tray trusted sources) to suppress browser security popups during print.\n- Generate ESC/POS or raw print payloads optimized for both 58mm and 80mm thermal paper widths.\n\n**Phase 3 — Settings & UX**\n- Add a **Print Method** toggle in the settings page: **Browser-native print** vs. **QZ Tray direct print**. Persist the user's preference.\n- Add a **Paper Size** selector (58mm / 80mm) in settings; persist preference.\n- Ensure all receipt previews and layouts adapt to the selected paper width (alignment, font scaling, line truncation, barcode/QR sizing).\n\n**Phase 4 — Fallback & Resilience**\n- Implement graceful fallback: if QZ Tray is unavailable, offline, or errors → fall back to the standard browser print dialog or PDF download.\n- Handle edge cases: printer offline, paper-out state, connection timeouts, multiple printers, and OS-level permission differences.\n\n**Phase 5 — Compatibility & Validation**\n- Test across Chrome, Firefox, Edge on Windows, macOS, and Linux (QZ Tray behavior varies by OS).\n- Verify printed output: text alignment, font legibility, barcode/QR scanability, and correct line truncation at 58mm / 80mm widths.\n- Confirm that existing **mobile** share flows (WhatsApp, email, image) remain intact and unaffected by the desktop-focused QZ Tray changes.\n- Validate that the settings page correctly saves, loads, and applies the paper size and print method preferences.",
