  "summary": "## Summary: QZ Tray Web — Audit & Standardize Receipt Print/Share\n\n### Changes Implemented\n- **Audited** all 13 files across the receipt print/share pipeline covering QZ Tray SDK v2.x integration (`qzTray.web.ts`), HTML receipt generation (`printReceipt.ts`, `receiptTemplates.ts`), report printing (`printReport.ts`), browser print fallback (`printHtmlBrowser.ts`), platform bridge (`qzTray.ts`), settings UI (`app/settings/print.tsx`), and transaksi-action trigger components (`bengkel/transaksi/index.tsx`, `TransactionDetailModal.tsx`).\n- **Fixed schema mismatch**: Added `print_method?: 'browser' | 'qz'` to the backend-facing `PrintSettings` interface in `services/settings.ts` so the user's print method preference persists to the server.\n- **Added backend sync**: Updated `handleSave` in `print.tsx` to include `print_method` when syncing local settings to the backend API.\n- **Added Print Method toggle UI**: Inserted a `Tabs` selector (Browser Native vs. QZ Tray Direct) in the settings page with contextual helper text explaining each method's behavior.\n- **Verified fallback chain**: `printReceipt.ts` already tries QZ Tray first, then gracefully falls back to `printHtmlInBrowser` (web) or BLE/expo-print (mobile).\n- **Verified mobile share flows intact**: `handleShareCreatedReceipt` in `bengkel/transaksi/index.tsx` and `handleShareLink` in `TransactionDetailModal.tsx` use `Share.share` / Web Clipboard API for WhatsApp/link sharing without interfering with thermal printing.\n\n### Files Modified\n- `frontend/services/settings.ts` — Added `print_method` field to `PrintSettings` interface\n- `frontend/app/settings/print.tsx` — Added print method toggle UI widget and backend `print_method` sync in save handler\n\n### Notes for Developer\n- QZ Tray integration currently uses HTML `pixel` mode (`format: 'html'`). This supports both 58mm/80mm paper widths through CSS width scaling. If thermal printing perf or alignment issues arise on specific printer models, consider migrating to raw ESC/POS sequences (`format: 'raw'`).\n- Default print method is `browser` if no preference is saved.\n- Certificate signing for QZ Tray is handled via `window.__QZ_SIGNING_URL` (set by backend config) with automatic fallback to QZ built-in self-signing.\n- Backend `settings` endpoint must accept the new `print_method` field. If the existing API has strict validation, the server-side Pydantic schema may need a minor update."
